{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3n5w6JJvh8DowJRhe5V","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I committed `data/2026-01.csv` as \"2026-01: add rows\", but the file has a bad row that the check didn't catch.\n\n**The check never looked at January.** `scripts/check.sh` printed \"OK\", but it only reads files for the year set in `scripts/check.conf`, which is `year=2025`. So it skipped `data/2026-01.csv`. I ran the same validation on the file by hand and it fails:\n\n- **Row 33:** `R2601-032,C117,399.31,wholesale` has 4 fields, but the header has 5 (`row_id,date,customer_id,amount,category`). The `date` value is missing.\n\nThis row came this way from `inbox/2026-01.csv`. The commit is only on your local `main`; nothing has been pushed.\n\n**Decision for you:**\n1. **Fill in the date** for row R2601-032, if you know it. I'll fix both the inbox and data copies and amend the commit.\n2. **Undo the commit** and wait for a corrected file from whoever supplies the inbox.\n\nThe cause is still there either way: every 2026 file will pass the check without being validated until `check.conf` changes. Setting `year=2026` would stop it checking the 2025 files. Changing the script to check every file in `data/` would cover both years. Which should I do?","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":16107,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":254,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-26>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:36:50.911Z","request_id":"gen-1794703005-LLEY0lI2VVUmzJodEbSs"}
